    "assumptions": [
      "Only the explicitly stated nonaccelerated Algorithm 1 is evaluated. The paper title emphasizes APIRL1-AM, but Algorithm 2 computes y without specifying its feedback into the printed z/u updates; that acceleration mechanism is not uniquely determined and is not claimed covered.",
      "The Eq. (12)/Algorithm 1 denominator is based on previous z, resolving the conflicting bar-z denominator in Eq. (11) by selecting the final explicit pseudocode.",
      "A three-pixel periodic 1D image is a deterministic finite-dimensional instance of the stated linear-operator model; K and gradient are explicitly supplied.",
      "epsilon=0.01 is an explicitly fixed positive smoothing value for numerical separation of threshold branches; no noise generation, clipping, continuation, FFT normalization or early stopping."
    ]
  },
